  "body": "### Problem\nThe `appModel` in BubbleTea is tightly coupled with synchronous data fetching. Keypresses in `update.go` directly invoke functions like `fetchArtistsPage`, intermingling UI update logic with network orchestration.\n\n### Solution\nExtract a `DataProvider` module that the TUI can use to asynchronously fetch data. The UI will just dispatch intent commands.\n\n**Proposed Interface:**\n```go\n// Using BubbleTea's Cmd pattern\ntype DataProvider interface {\n    FetchTopArtists(timeRange string) tea.Cmd\n    FetchTopSongs(timeRange string) tea.Cmd\n    FetchArtistsPage(url string) tea.Cmd\n    FetchSongsPage(url string) tea.Cmd\n}\n```\n\n### Benefits\n* **Locality:** The `appModel.Update` function focuses entirely on state transitions and key handling.\n* **Leverage:** The TUI gains leverage by simply requesting commands and waiting for the resulting `tea.Msg` (e.g., `switchToArtistsMsg`).\n* **Testing:** The UI state machine can be tested in isolation by supplying a fake `DataProvider` that instantly returns predefined `tea.Msg`s.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Create the `DataProvider` interface.\n- [ ] Refactor the switch cases in `update.go` to use the `DataProvider` instead of calling fetch functions directly.\n- [ ] Ensure BubbleTea's command patterns are properly utilized for async fetching.\n",
